e package says. Drain and lay them out on an oiled tray so they don’t stick.","uses":[0]},{"text":"Wilt the spinach in a dry skillet or the microwave, then squeeze out as much liquid as you can and chop it.","uses":[1]},{"text":"Mix the spinach, ricotta, egg, grated cheese, half the mozzarella, garlic, salt and nutmeg.","uses":[2,3,4,5,6,7,8]},{"text":"Spread 1 cup of the sauce in the baking dish. Fill each shell with a heaping spoonful of the mixture and nestle them side by side. Spoon the rest of the sauce over and scatter with the remaining mozzarella.","uses":[9]},{"text":"Cover with foil and bake for {time 20 min}, then uncover and bake until bubbling and the cheese is golden, {time 10-15 min}. Scatter with basil.","uses":[10]}]}